	"Description": "Now you can place grass to make your entire farm green! It even changes with the seasons. :D\n<br />\n<br />[code][size=5]Install[/size][list=1]\n<br />[*][url=https://smapi.io]Install the latest version of SMAPI[/url].\n<br />[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/1915]Install Content Patcher[/url].\n<br />[*]Download this mod and unzip it into [font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/Mods[/font].\n<br />[*]Run the game using SMAPI.\n<br />[/list]\n<br />\n<br />I checked, and amusingly you can run all of them at once if your heart desires. The three do not stack despite looking identical.\n<br />[/code]\n<br />\n<br />[s]~Minor Bug~\n<br />The name on the crafting menu is still \"Gravel Path\". (still \"Straw Floor\" in alt download) I'd have to code more to fix it. It will be done eventually, but I wanted to release this for enjoyment until then.\n<br />\n<br />~Alt file bug~\n<br />If you buy the Straw Floor recipe after installing the mod it seems to disappear without adding it to the craft screen. Trying to figure out if this is a problem on my end or something with the Beta.\n<br />[/s]\n<br />With 1.6, I took the time to do this right. I had been having an issue with bought paths, so I figured I'd just upload versions for whichever flooring you start with that you like. I don't know how to change out footsteps sounds, so that's the real reason for multiple files.",
